course: dictionary
lesson: 335
title: Ankylosaurus: the armoured dinosaur
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A dictionary tells you what a word means, and the sentences show it in use. Ankylosaurus is a long word, but the clues around it help. «Ankylosaurus was covered with bony plates in its skin.» Bony plates are hard, like armour, so this tells you the dinosaur was well protected.
explain: The entry says it had a heavy club at the end of its tail. «It swung a heavy bony tail club that could break a leg bone.» Swung and break are clues: the club was a weapon for defence, not something used to pick up food.
explain: Good readers join clues together. «Ankylosaurus was a living tank, covered in bony plates.» A tank is hard to hurt, so the author is comparing the dinosaur to a tank to show how strongly it was protected.
fact: An ankylosaurus was a large, plant-eating dinosaur.
fact: «Ankylosaurus» means a dinosaur covered in thick bony plates, like armour.
fact: Its tail ended in a heavy club, which it could swing to defend itself.
fact: It lived at the end of the age of dinosaurs (the Late Cretaceous), in what is now North America.
fact: A «tail club» is the heavy bony end of the tail, and an «armoured dinosaur» is one covered in plates for protection.
exercise: «Ankylosaurus was covered with bony plates in its skin.» What were the plates like? | Soft and furry | Bright and see-through | Made of glass | *Hard, like armour
exercise: What was at the end of an ankylosaurus's tail? | *A heavy club | A feathery fan | A soft cushion | A long, thin whip
exercise: The entry says ankylosaurus was a large, plant-eating dinosaur. What did it eat? | Fish | Meat | *Plants | Insects
test: Why did the ankylosaurus need its armour? | *To defend itself from meat eaters | To fly faster | To keep its colour bright | To float in water
test: Ankylosaurus lived at the end of the age of dinosaurs. Where did it live? | Europe | Australia | *North America | Antarctica
exam: Which sentence best describes an ankylosaurus? | A small, fast, feathered bird | A sea creature with fins | A tall dinosaur with a long neck | *A large, armoured, plant-eating dinosaur with a tail club
